{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\nfor f in ['data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/approved-plan.json','docs/design/research/standards-support.json']:\n d=json.loads(pathlib.Path(f).read_text()); print(f,list(d) if isinstance(d,dict) else 'list');\n if 'standards' in f: print(json.dumps(d,ensure_ascii=False)[:5000])\nprint('missing',[(p,pathlib.Path(p).exists()) for p in ['scripts/corporate_financing_v1.py','scripts/check_accounting_p08.py','tests/test_accounting_p08.py','data/accounting-master/deliverables/P08/authority-and-methods.json','data/accounting-master/deliverables/P08/result.md']])\nPY\nrg -n 'MC06|MC15|MC17|MC19|MC29|MC30' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\"","aggregated_output":"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/approved-plan.json ['plan', 'review', 'plan_hash']\ndocs/design/research/standards-support.json ['records', 'blocked']\n{\"records\": [{\"id\": \"aasb102\", \"url\": \"https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB102_07-15.pdf\", \"path\": \"docs/design/research/standards/aasb102.pdf\", \"sha256\": \"0d6fb4f59cc6daa7088f25e73542945d346f9c737ca85abf1a164a332bf93c06\", \"access_date\": \"2026-10-02\", \"inspected\": \"Comparison with IAS 2; paragraphs 23–27, 28–34\", \"support_scope\": \"Official Australian adoption; for-profit relevant common text; not a claim about all later amendments\", \"edition_applicability\": \"July 2015 issue; paragraph 40 applies to annual periods beginning on or after 2018-01-01, with the stated earlier-application provisions. Later amendments not checked in this pass.\", \"edition_pages\": [1, 10], \"preparation_dossiers\": \"docs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/\"}, {\"id\": \"aasb17\", \"url\": \"https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB17_07-17_COMPdec22_01-23.pdf\", \"path\": \"docs/design/research/standards/aasb17.pdf\", \"sha256\": \"153e720cc1eaf7eea47d50463003391ea0433271694dd83a44c54a0e92deaec3\", \"access_date\": \"2026-10-02\", \"inspected\": \"Comparison with IFRS17; paragraphs 14–24, 32–38, 53–59, 60–70A, 78–82, B126–B127; reinspection of PAA, separate reinsurance recognition/eligibility, presentation and period applicability on 2 October 2026\", \"support_scope\": \"Official compiled text; PAA service, gross/ceded and risk-adjustment examples only; no full compliance\", \"edition_applicability\": \"Annual periods beginning on or after 2023-01-01 and before 2026-07-01; compiled amendments through 2022-12-15. Applicability uses period start, not the date of this review.\", \"edition_pages\": [1, 5], \"preparation_dossiers\": \"docs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/\"}, {\"id\": \"aasb132\", \"url\": \"https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB132_08-15_COMPdec22_01-23.pdf\", \"path\": \"docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.pdf\", \"sha256\": \"5c8ce25447c6186ec49f751bc9e7ad48563caaff542b0e0287f3f7783a480501\", \"access_date\": \"2026-10-02\", \"inspected\": \"Comparison with IAS32; paragraphs 15–22, 28–32, AG30–AG35\", \"support_scope\": \"Official compiled text; issuer compound split and maturity conversion; other classification conditions must be checked\", \"edition_applicability\": \"Annual periods beginning on or after 2023-01-01 and before 2026-07-01; compiled amendments through 2022-12-15. Applicability uses period start, not the date of this review.\", \"edition_pages\": [1, 5], \"preparation_dossiers\": \"docs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/\"}, {\"id\": \"asbe-reproduction\", \"url\": \"https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/企业会计准则第1号——存货\", \"path\": \"docs/design/research/standards/asbe-reproduction.html\", \"sha256\": \"ef50c4730a0c81f16ee419d63f6cade854dbc9a6a254938d05eeb9d920ebebd6\", \"access_date\": \"2026-10-02\", \"inspected\": \"Entire reproduced 2006 text, articles 1–22, particularly 14–19\", \"support_scope\": \"Unofficial reproduction attributed to Ministry of Finance; official origin/version verification remains pending\", \"preparation_dossiers\": \"docs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/\"}, {\"id\": \"caterpillar2024\", \"url\": \"https://www.annualreports.com/HostedData/AnnualReportArchive/c/NYSE_CAT_2024.pdf\", \"path\": \"docs/design/research/standards/caterpillar2024.pdf\", \"sha256\": \"3a38651c724016bca792bef165fd42bb09d9b033d23718372a2599378768e925\", \"access_date\": \"2026-10-02\", \"inspected\": \"Note 1.C inventories and Note 8 inventories; note number corrected against the retained PDF on 2 October 2026\", \"support_scope\": \"Company-authored report, mirror download; records disclosed US-GAAP LIFO policy, not full ASC330 authority\", \"preparation_dossiers\": \"docs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/\"}], \"blocked\": [{\"source\": \"FASB ASU2015-11 official PDF\", \"reason\": \"403 in default and elevated requests; DART ASC330 primary text requires login; no bypass attempted\"}, {\"source\": \"Ministry of Finance standards index\", \"reason\": \"502 in default and elevated requests; unofficial text retained with verification pending\"}]}\nmissing [('scripts/corporate_financing_v1.py', False), ('scripts/check_accounting_p08.py', False), ('tests/test_accounting_p08.py', False), ('data/accounting-master/deliverables/P08/authority-and-methods.json', False), ('data/accounting-master/deliverables/P08/result.md', False)]\n60:| MC06 | Distinguish legal entities, ownership, control, group perimeter and consolidation. U1, D. | Provide dated entity/control and adjustment-book types, acquisition/disposal and intragroup examples, and rules preventing unexplained consolidation plugs. | Specified structural control/elimination model; Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` check a simplified 80% acquisition, intragroup loan and full disposal. Actual control conclusions, goodwill/tax/FX and complex retained interests need further authority and operations. G4, G7, G12. |\n79:| MC15 | Specify ordinary corporate operations and accounting across periods. U1, U2, U3, D. | Provide a bounded coherent package for revenue/collections, purchases/payments, inventory/costs, assets/depreciation, payroll, financing and applicable closing/tax assumptions, with explicit exclusions. | Specified bounded corporate package in Chs. 2, 8 with exact annual/interim and forecast fixtures. Delivery, collection, purchase, payment, costs, plant, payroll, debt, simple tax and closing reconcile. Real tax/revenue/lease/FX packages remain separate work. G4, G5. |\n81:| MC17 | Represent financing instruments and their economic/accounting lifecycles, particularly bonds and equity. U1, U2, D. | Specify proceeds, principal, carrying/fair values, rates, calendars, maturities, rights and share quantities; work issuance, accrual, settlement and relevant modification/conversion/default cases under declared treatments. | Partially specified and reference-checked: Chs. 8–9 distinguish principal/carrying/fair values and work ordinary and convertible bond issue, accrual, redemption/conversion, shares and funding default. Detailed modification, early repurchase and other-basis hybrid classification remain open. G4, G7. |\n88:| MC19 | Accommodate IFRS, US GAAP and China GAAP/ASBE with dated treatments, elections and transitions. U1, U3. | Define the supported treatment matrix, rule authority and version selection; show matched economic events under selected genuinely different treatments and identify unimplemented operations. | Partially repaired. Ch. 9 compares FIFO/LIFO/average and records dated rule selection. Selected IAS-equivalent paragraphs inspected in official AASB texts; US LIFO has company-policy evidence only, full ASC authority is blocked, and official ASBE version verification remains pending. Source dossiers record exact edition/period limits and correct Caterpillar inventories to Note 8. G7, G8, G13. The acquired panel now supplies report-level preparation-basis evidence across US GAAP, IFRS-oriented reporting and ASBE; this does not replace dated primary accounting authority. |\n108:| MC29 | Conduct a broad, technically grounded literature survey beyond the original collection. U3, P. | Inspect relevant primary methods/theory/evaluation/appendices and official code where available; compare direct alternatives; make genuine backward/forward screening, source-specific omissions, corrections and claim support inspectable. | Partially repaired: 179 individual title/metadata decisions across 194 occurrences/72 searches replace generic exclusions; generation rejects unscreened candidates. Mack and selected rule sources add inspected technical support. All-candidate full-text review and later module literature are not complete. G8. |\n109:| MC30 | Preserve the relevant source library and precise provenance. U3, P. | Archive accessible relevant papers under the required naming convention, retain exact versions/anchors, preserve original files, and document unavailable sources without relying on their uninspected claims. | 32 catalogued paper PDFs verified by hash/page count, with original collection preserved; Apple filings and selected standards archived separately. Version/authority limits and four blocked papers remain recorded. Mechanical integrity does not certify every technical claim. G8. The additional financial-report corpus preserves 244 original versions, source/index/discovery hashes and an append-only attempt history; 192 target slots pass source acceptance. |\n140:plan; v1 evidence remains preserved. This advances MC01, MC03, MC05, MC19–22,\n141:MC28, MC30 and MC33–35 without closing semantic, accounting or forecast\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p data/accounting-master/deliverables/P08 docs/design/research/p08-v1\ncat > data/accounting-master/deliverables/P08/progress.md <<'EOF'\n# P08 implementation checkpoint\n\n2026-10-03. Recovery and structured approved plan/review inspected. The two\nrequired deliverables, engine, checker and test file are absent. Prior stopped\nplanning work supplies no implementation evidence. Approved scope is a synthetic\nissuer compound convertible bond; MC06/15/17/19/29/30 and G4/G7/G8 stay wider.\n\n## Pre-execution skeptical audit and evidence contract\n\nQuestion: can applicable primary authority support a parameterized, exact issuer\nlifecycle and same-fact comparison? Comparator: existing compound-bond dossier\n(arithmetic regression only), independently derived present values and cash flows.\nPass: inspected applicable recognition/measurement/classification/settlement\nanchors, parameterized atomic journals, both multi-period settlements, matched\ninputs and reproducible notes. Vetoes: unsupported authority blocks the affected\ntreatment; invalid dates, ineligible terms, imbalance, negative funding or state\nmismatch block implementation acceptance. Source failures do not stop independent\npreparation. No short check establishes accounting compliance, forecast validity,\nhuman acceptance, superiority or whole-gap closure. Result and source/hash evidence\nwill be preserved in authority-and-methods.json and result.md.\n\nDefaults audit: annual periods, two coupons, fixed shares, functional currency,\nno fees/tax/options and 10% comparable yield come from the reviewed synthetic\nexample (hypotheses, not real-market estimates). Wrong eligibility or yield can\nproduce balanced but wrong accounting: reject unsupported clauses and independently\ncheck PV, alternative parameters and authority applicability. Australian for-profit\nTier 1 basis is a bounded scope choice; check edition and period-start limits.\nOpening cash/equity 20 is synthetic settlement funding; test insufficient cash and\natomic rollback. Exact rational arithmetic is an engineering choice; this does not\nvalidate real currency rounding. Inspection dates do not substitute for effective\nperiods. Matched comparisons hold economics fixed; absent sources stay unresolved.\n\nAudit passes for this bounded plan: no ranking/proxy promotion, source-dependent\nstops are local, and exact outputs answer only the stated conformance question.\n\n## Files and next steps\n\nDeclared new files: scripts/corporate_financing_v1.py,\nscripts/check_accounting_p08.py, tests/test_accounting_p08.py,\ndocs/design/research/p08-v1/*, and the three permitted P08 files. Existing dossier,\nshared engines, frozen corpus and protected supervisor files remain preserved.\nNext: inspect applicable AASB 9, AASB 132 and a legitimate primary comparator;\nrecord source-specific access outcomes; implement engine, generate cases, test\nnegative paths and run unittest plus checker --check. All deliverables unfinished.\nEOF\npython3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib,hashlib,json\np=pathlib.Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/phase-entry-inventory.json')\nd=json.loads(p.read_text()); print('Inventory entries',len(d))\nfor f in ['AGENTS.md','docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.pdf','docs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/compound-bond.md']:\n print(f,hashlib.sha256(pathlib.Path(f).read_bytes()).hexdigest())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
